    "text": "For any positive integer&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math>, define <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>:</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#8734;</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>R</mi></math> as<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mo>&#8721;</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msup><mi>tan</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></mfenced><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfrac></mfenced></math> for all <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#8734;</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> .</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo></math>Here, the inverse trigonometric function <math><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">tan</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>&#8289;</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></math> assumes values in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>)</mo></math></p><p>Then, which of the following statement(s) is (are) TRUE?</p>",
